# Pre-delivery quality gates

Do not declare work done or return a completion answer until all four gates pass locally — the same gates CI runs:

1. `pnpm typecheck`
2. `pnpm lint`
3. `pnpm format:check`
4. `pnpm test` (or `pnpm coverage` when the change can affect coverage thresholds)

```
# ❌ BAD
pnpm test && echo "CI will catch lint"
# or: skip format:check; “we can format later”

# ✅ GOOD
pnpm typecheck && pnpm lint && pnpm format:check && pnpm test
# fix failures, re-run the gates, then answer
```

If any command fails: fix, re-run the failing gate (and the others if the fix could affect them), then answer. Do not finish with “CI will catch it”, “format later”, or “tests later”.

**Out of scope for the gate** (no need to run the four commands): questions, plan-only discussion, and changes that cannot affect TS/lint/format/tests (copy-only catalog edits still run `check:i18n` per the i18n rule). This rule does not replace `.cursor/rules/test-coverage.mdc`.
